    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/12/asics-gel-nimbus-28-review-2026.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Max-stack build delivers strong impact protection and near-zero ground feel, but the ride is firmer/stiffer than expected; heel feels balanced between firm and soft, while the forefoot is firmer and stiffer.",
        "Responsiveness: Firmer tuning with a snappy forefoot and lighter weight improves uptempo capability and transitions, but it is more snappy than truly bouncy.",
        "Stability: Highly stable-neutral setup from a wide, firmer platform, sidewalls, sole flare, filled midfoot, and stiff construction; heel counter is stiff and supportive.",
        "Durability: Less outsole rubber and more exposed midsole reduce confidence in long-term wear; early forefoot outsole wear is visible by ~55 miles with concern about potential heel rubber peeling, suggesting average durability."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2026/01/ryans-asics-gel-nimbus-28-review-6.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The high stack (43.5 mm heel / 35.5 mm forefoot) gives strong long-run impact protection, but the FF Blast+ setup feels more firm than plush and the forefoot can feel flat/slappy.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is moderate at best; the ride is described as low-rebound, not very bouncy, and lacking snappy toe-off, with a blocky feel at faster paces.",
        "Stability: A wide platform, stiff heel-to-toe construction, supportive upper containment, and a solid rearfoot build produce a guided, stable neutral ride with good lateral support.",
        "Durability: Upper/build quality is robust, but durability concerns center on minimal forefoot rubber coverage, early heel outsole wear, and midfoot foam graining after only a few runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/asics-nimbus-28-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Very plush and soft FF Blast Plus foam with noticeable compression and strong impact protection from the high stack; heel and forefoot feel smooth and forgiving rather than firm.",
        "Responsiveness: Comfort is prioritized over energy return, with the ride described as not springy or energetic and lacking snappy rebound.",
        "Stability: No explicit torsional rigidity or heel-counter detail is given, but the ride is characterized as blocky and predictable with sufficient lateral support for easy running and walking.",
        "Durability: The unchanged hybrid AsicsGrip + AHAR Plus outsole is called predictably durable with reliable traction, suggesting solid outsole wear resistance and material longevity."
      ]
    }
